    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-5998: f'(x)=x/4-1/x, so the arc-length integrand on [1,4] is x/4+1/x; integration gives ln(4)+15/8. q-82616: differentiating sqrt(2)-arcsin(x) gives -1/sqrt(1-x²), whose square produces the stated integrand. q-82639: differentiating -2sqrt(x³) on [0,1] gives -3sqrt(x), whose square is 9x. q-42153: R₂←R₂-3R₁ gives echelon rows (1,3,2) and (0,0,0), hence x=2-3y with y arbitrary. q-73751: scaling R₁ by 1/5 and subtracting 2R₁ from R₂ gives rows (1,-2,-1) and (0,0,4), so the system is inconsistent. q-126458: D-C=(-6,2,7), giving the selected line through C. q-162161: the starting point requires a=3, the displacement Q-P requires b=1, and the segment starts at c=0; their sum is 4. q-72725 and q-43078: a row swap reverses the determinant sign, giving 69 and -105. q-130730 and q-130729: scaling one row scales the determinant by the same factor, giving -12 and 16. q-130740 and q-130739: det(kA)=k^n det(A), giving -100 and -128. q-130742: the row swap reverses the sign and the row addition leaves it unchanged, giving -23. q-130743: row addition leaves the determinant unchanged and the subsequent row scaling divides it by 3, giving 7. q-130857: the displayed X indeed has determinant -60; Y swaps its first and third rows, giving 60. No prior answer or captured grade was supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
